        <title>Waterbody_Lakes_Scale_5Million_to_300000</title>
        <abstract>All features have been included from the Surface Hydrology data capture. 250K Specification Description - Lake - A naturally occurring body of mainly static water surrounded by land. (Source - http://www.ga.gov.au/mapspecs/topographic/v6/appendixA_files/Waterbodies.html). NOTE - This layer only displays between 1:5,050,000 and 1:300,001 scales and a size criteria of area greater than 0.003 map units to avoid clutter at the national scale (approx 1:36,000,000). Refer to other Waterbody - Lake layers at different scales for the National Map.</abstract>
